Fixed. The bug was in `src/resources/storage.ts` — `clampToStorageCap` clamped wood and stone with `Math.min(..., cap)` but passed food through untouched, so only food (the only resource with passive production that can exceed cap via a farm surplus) kept climbing past storehouse limits.

Changes:
- `src/resources/storage.ts:25` — `food` is now clamped with `Math.min(resources.food, cap)` like the other two kinds; updated the two doc comments that referenced the buggy food case.
- `tests/settlement.test.ts` — added regression coverage: `clampToStorageCap` clamps food to the cap (and never raises below-cap resources), and `advanceTurn` pins food at 50 across consecutive turns instead of letting it grow unbounded.

Verified: `npm test` — all 18 tests pass (14 pre-existing + 4 new), `tsc --noEmit` clean. No other code path bypasses the cap: raid/drought only decrease resources, and building/repair/upgrade costs only deduct.


